# Compiled binaries. Nim writes one beside its source with no extension, so
# these ignore anything here without a dot in its name rather than listing the
# executables by hand: a list only covers the sources that exist today, and the
# binary a throwaway probe leaves behind is never on it.
#
# Directories are put back, because ignoring them by the same rule would drop a
# whole subdirectory of test data without saying so - git reports nothing when
# an add matches an ignored path. Only files are meant to be caught here.
#
# This block comes FIRST and every general rule below it comes after, because a
# later rule wins: putting directories back here would otherwise re-admit each
# build directory the rules below exclude - nimcache, build, __pycache__, the
# .app bundle `nimble app_debug` writes - since those are directories too. A
# negation is only as narrow as what follows it.
tests/*
!tests/*.*
!tests/*/
examples/*
!examples/*.*
!examples/*/

nimcache/
nimblecache/
htmldocs/
build/
.venv/

__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.vscode/
*.pyc

.DS_Store
*.app
*.dSYM
